diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2ec8833
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,198 @@
+Feature: TodoMVC todos
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Creating todos
+
+    Scenario: Create a new todo
+      Given the new todo input contains "Buy milk"
+      When I press Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the new item reads "Buy milk"
+      And the new todo input is cleared
+
+    Scenario: Ignore empty input when creating a todo
+      Given the new todo input is empty
+      When I press Enter
+      Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Trim whitespace from new todo input
+      Given the new todo input contains "  Buy milk  "
+      When I press Enter
+      Then the new item reads "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Displaying the todo list
+
+    Scenario: Hide main and footer when no todos exist
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      Then main section is not visible
+      And footer section is not visible
+
+    Scenario: Show main and footer when todos exist
+      Given the todo list contains 1 item
+      Then main section is visible
+      And footer section is visible
+
+  Rule: Marking todos as complete
+
+    Scenario: Mark a todo as complete
+      Given the todo list contains 1 item
+      When I click the checkbox on the item
+      Then the item has class "completed"
+
+    Scenario: Mark a todo as active
+      Given the todo list contains a completed item
+      When I click the checkbox on the item
+      Then the item does not have class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Toggle all todos
+
+    Scenario: Mark all todos as complete
+      Given the todo list contains 3 active items
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all items have class "completed"
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Mark all todos as active
+      Given the todo list contains 3 completed items
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then no items have class "completed"
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox reflects individual item state
+      Given the todo list contains 3 items
+      When I mark all items as complete individually
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed resets toggle-all checkbox
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active and 2 completed items
+      When I click "Clear completed"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Removing todos
+
+    Scenario: Remove a todo
+      Given the todo list contains 1 item
+      When I click the destroy button on the item
+      Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+  Rule: Editing todos
+
+    Scenario: Activate editing mode
+      Given the todo list contains 1 item
+      When I double-click the item label
+      Then the item has class "editing"
+      And the edit input contains the item title
+      And the edit input is focused
+
+    Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+      Given the item is in editing mode
+      When I type "Buy groceries" in the edit input
+      And I press Enter in the edit input
+      Then the item reads "Buy groceries"
+      And the item does not have class "editing"
+
+    Scenario: Save edit on blur
+      Given the item is in editing mode
+      When I type "Buy groceries" in the edit input
+      And the edit input loses focus
+      Then the item reads "Buy groceries"
+      And the item does not have class "editing"
+
+    Scenario: Destroy todo when edit text is empty
+      Given the item is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input
+      And I press Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Destroy todo when edit text is only whitespace
+      Given the item is in editing mode
+      When I type "   " in the edit input
+      And I press Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Cancel editing on Escape
+      Given the item is in editing mode and the title is "Buy milk"
+      When I type "Buy groceries" in the edit input
+      And I press Escape in the edit input
+      Then the item reads "Buy milk"
+      And the item does not have class "editing"
+
+  Rule: Item count
+
+    Scenario: Show the number of active items
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active item
+      Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Pluralize item count
+      Given the todo list contains 2 active items
+      Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Show zero items left
+      Given the todo list contains 2 completed items
+      Then the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active and 2 completed items
+      When I click "Clear completed"
+      Then the todo list has 1 item
+      And that item is active
+
+    Scenario: Hide clear completed when no completed todos
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active item
+      Then the clear-completed button is not visible
+
+  Rule: Persistence
+
+    Scenario: Persist todos to localStorage
+      Given the todo list contains 1 item titled "Buy milk"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the item reads "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: Persist todo completion state
+      Given the todo list contains 1 completed item titled "Buy milk"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the item has class "completed"
+
+    Scenario: Persist active filter across reloads
+      Given the filter "#/active" is selected
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the "#/active" filter has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Routing and filtering
+
+    Scenario: Show all todos by default
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active and 1 completed item
+      When the app loads
+      Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+    Scenario: Filter to active todos
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active and 1 completed item
+      When I click the "Active" filter link
+      Then the "Active" filter has class "selected"
+      And the todo list shows 1 active item
+
+    Scenario: Filter to completed todos
+      Given the todo list contains 1 active and 1 completed item
+      When I click the "Completed" filter link
+      Then the "Completed" filter has class "selected"
+      And the todo list shows 1 completed item
+
+    Scenario: Hide item when it no longer matches the active filter
+      Given the "Active" filter is selected
+      And the todo list contains 1 active item
+      When I mark the item as complete
+      Then the item is not visible in the list
+
+    Scenario: Hide item when it no longer matches the completed filter
+      Given the "Completed" filter is selected
+      And the todo list contains 1 completed item
+      When I mark the item as active
+      Then the item is not visible in the list
